.TH HALCYON-HOST 1 "November 2026" "Halcyon 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
halcyon-host \- run the Halcyon host-mode modem service
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B halcyon-host
[\fIoptions\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Starts the two loopback TCP ports that host-mode clients drive: 8300 for
CR-terminated commands and events, 8301 for the link's byte stream.  PAT and
other clients that speak this command set connect there; the default addresses
match what PAT expects.
.PP
The service runs in the foreground and stops on SIGINT or SIGTERM.  Bytes a
client writes to the data port are carried through the modem and returned
decoded, which makes the path testable without a second station.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-\-host " " \fIADDRESS\fR
Address to bind.  Default \fB127.0.0.1\fR; keep it on the loopback interface.
.TP
.BR \-\-cmd\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Command port.  Default \fB8300\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-data\-port " " \fIPORT\fR
Data port.  Default \fB8301\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-mycall " " \fICALL\fR
Callsign reported before the client sends \fBMYCALL\fR.  Default \fBN0CALL\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-bandwidth " " \fI500|2300|2750\fR
Default bandwidth selector.  \fB500\fR selects the robust profile; \fB2300\fR and
\fB2750\fR select the wide profile.  A \fBBW...\fR command from the client
overrides it.  Default \fB2300\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-snr " " \fIDB\fR
Simulated link signal-to-noise ratio.  Default \fB10\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-channel " " \fIawgn|good|moderate|poor\fR
Simulated channel.  Default \fBawgn\fR.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-echo
Do not return decoded data to the client that wrote it.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.cache/halcyon/host.log
Output when started by \fBhalcyon-switch on\fR.
.SH EXAMPLES
Run the service for PAT on the ports PAT expects:
.PP
.nf
.RS
halcyon-host --mycall N0CALL --bandwidth 2300
.RE
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR halcyon (1),
.BR halcyon-switch (1)
.PP
Setup guide: \fI/usr/share/doc/halcyon/PAT.md\fR.
